+{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_01Nx8kPNeTEh6LmWxCZWfjo4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017stfFjCQ9HfsXdsu1mmFbF","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/CONTRACT.md","content":"# Contract: Constraint-Based Event Scheduler\n\n## Behaviors and Verification\n\n- [ ] `schedule` is exported from `src/index.ts` (named export) → test: `import { schedule } from '../src/index'` works and is a function.\n- [ ] Basic scheduling: a single event with no constraints, within window → assigned a room, `startTime >= options.startTime`, `endTime = startTime + duration <= options.endTime`. Ends up in `assignments`, not in `unscheduled`.\n- [ ] Multiple independent events fit in separate rooms simultaneously (no forced serialization when rooms are available) → test: 2 events, 2 rooms, both scheduled, can overlap in time since different rooms.\n- [ ] Room capacity: event with `attendees` greater than every room's `capacity` → event lands in `unscheduled`, not `assignments`.\n- [ ] Room capacity: event fits only in the larger of two rooms → assigned to that room specifically (never assigned to a room whose capacity < attendees).\n- [ ] Time window: no assignment has `startTime < options.startTime` or `endTime > options.endTime`.\n- [ ] Window too small: event duration longer than `endTime - startTime` → `unscheduled`.\n- [ ] Room gap: two events in the same room respect `endTime[first] + gap <= startTime[second]` for the configured (or default 15) gap.\n- [ ] Room gap default: when `options.gap` omitted, default of 15 minutes is enforced between same-room events.\n- [ ] Room gap custom: a custom `gap` value (e.g., 30) is enforced instead of the default.\n- [ ] Prerequisites ordering: event B with `prerequisites: ['A']` is scheduled such that `assignments[A].endTime + gap <= assignments[B].startTime`.\n- [ ] Prerequisites with multiple deps: event C depending on both A and B starts after the later of the two (+gap).\n- [ ] Prerequisite chain across rooms: prerequisite ordering is enforced even when A and B end up in different rooms.\n- [ ] Unschedulable prerequisite cascades: if a prerequisite event cannot itself be scheduled (e.g. capacity impossible), the dependent event also ends up in `unscheduled` (never violates ordering by scheduling anyway).\n- [ ] Preferred room honored: when an event's `preferredRoom` can accommodate it without violating other constraints, it is assigned to that room.\n- [ ] Preferred room overridden when infeasible: when the preferred room lacks capacity or has no free slot in the window, the event is still scheduled in a different valid room rather than left unscheduled.\n- [ ] Cycle detection: direct self-reference (`A` lists `A` as a prerequisite) → `schedule(...)` throws an `Error`.\n- [ ] Cycle detection: multi-node cycle (`A -> B -> A`) → throws an `Error`.\n- [ ] No false positives: a valid DAG of prerequisites (e.g., diamond shape A -> B, A -> C, B -> D, C -> D) does not throw and schedules successfully.\n- [ ] Batch optimization / maximize count: given a choice between fitting one long event or several short events in the remaining room-time, the scheduler prefers the option that maximizes total scheduled event count (e.g., input order lists the long event first, but the algorithm still fits the short ones instead of naively blocking on the long one first).\n- [ ] Unscheduled list correctness: every event id that is not present in `assignments` appears exactly once in `unscheduled`, and vice versa (assignments + unscheduled together account for all input events, no duplicates, no omissions).\n- [ ] No overlapping assignments in the same room even accounting for gap (validated generically over randomized/generated test cases).\n\n## Verification commands\n- `npm test` — vitest test suite covering all criteria above.\n- `npm run build` — `tsc` compiles with no errors.\n- `npm run lint` — `eslint src/` passes with no errors.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":724,"cache_read_input_tokens":45197,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":724},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69bcc0c6-ca5b-44ec-bdb3-183457e76ff4","uuid":"5db86455-fe0c-47c5-873d-46e2644eff81","request_id":"req_011CcaVbdEsqb74wtuvhkf8w"}
